# Documentation only. Inject values through the server process environment.
# Do not store real JWT_SIGNING_SECRET or account passwords in .env.
# JWT_SIGNING_SECRET: required for Go/Flask Token auth; at least 32 random bytes.
# SEED_TEACHER_A_PASSWORD: password for teacher_a during first initialization.
# SEED_STUDENT_A1_PASSWORD: password for student_a1 during first initialization.
# SEED_TEACHER_B_PASSWORD: password for teacher_b during first initialization.
# SEED_STUDENT_B1_PASSWORD: password for student_b1 during first initialization.
# MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES: optional positive file-size limit; default is 20 MiB.
# Token authentication does not use SECRET_KEY or COOKIE_SECURE. Use HTTPS in production.

# Default Go Compose (no SECRET_KEY required):
# INITIALIZATION_MODE: explicitly fresh or migrate; there is no implicit default.
# fresh: prepare schema and seed an empty target using all four SEED_* passwords.
# Repeated fresh verifies its receipt/data without resetting passwords or files.
# migrate: only accept an already imported/verified migration receipt and data;
# never import or seed automatically. Stop the app before any offline operation.
# Existing unknown/nonempty targets are refused, never reset.
# DB_PASSWORD: required application database password, inject via environment.
# MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: required initialization password, inject via environment.
# DEV_HTTP_PORT: optional loopback Nginx port, default 8081.
# GOPROXY: optional build-only Go module proxy; defaults to proxy.golang.org,direct.
# GO_IMAGE / GO_INIT_IMAGE: optional distinct server/initializer image tags.
# Use a new explicit Compose project; do not reuse Flask RAG Demo projects/volumes.
# Recreate containers while retaining volumes; do not run two app writers sharing uploads.
# Legacy Flask Compose: docker compose -f docker-compose.legacy.yml ...
